lines=['# Round-five handoff','',f'PR: https://github.com/crvouga/gamezilla/pull/280',f'Source SHA: `{m["candidateSha"]}`',f'Media SHA: `{media}`',f'Evidence code: `{m["evidence_code"]}`',f'Build SHA-256: `{m["buildSha256"]}`','',m['status'],'',m['publicStatus'],'','## Source and integration','', 'All intended worker changes and the integration fixes are committed. Ownership was reconciled against the actual diff and unique handoffs; the generic BOARD handoff and mislabeled chess/Pong handoffs were not used as authoritative source descriptions. See SOURCE_REVIEW.md and intended-source-paths.json.','', 'Integration preserves saved puzzle completion separately from the current Sokoban board, including movement and restart after solving. Numberlink uses its existing enclosing Next/Pack controls. Shared desktop rails and phone chip facts are compact, Quoridor controls avoid wrapping, rack corners retain hit coverage, and fitted WordTiles workbench boards stay within the initial viewport while enlarged cells keep their precision size. Hosted follow-up repairs restore the exhaustive chess guidance-placement proof, all Numberlink/Sokoban saved-completion consumers and the accessible Pong rally status used by real physics journeys. Battleship secondary target tools retain pre-scroll viewport fit. Literal regressions and known-bug entries accompany the fixes. Readiness rows were updated.','', '## Automated verification','']
for name,outcome in v.items():lines.append(f'- **{name}:** {outcome}')
lines += ['', 'Native readiness/play, geometry, browser errors, accessibility and pixel outcomes are distinct. No macOS references were accepted. No assertion tolerances, retries, skips or specs were changed to suppress failures. The initial failing runs and the orchestration interruptions remain in interactions/. The first full matrix ran against an earlier dirty build; it is diagnostic evidence, not the final candidate verdict.','', '## Canonical Ubuntu','',json.dumps(m['ubuntu'],indent=2),'','## Media','',f'{m["storyCount"]} selected stories across all 14 boards plus shared-frame and related component references; {m["screenshots"]} after PNGs and {m["pairs"]} pairs against round-four before images. New states without a round-four predecessor are explicitly labeled.',f'{m["videoCount"]} videos cover {m["videoJourneys"]} bounded journeys at phone 390×844 and desktop 1440×900. Screenshots cover both themes; native checks use 390×844 and 1440×844. Animated PR previews sample full recordings at 2 fps. Recorder pacing is automated, not natural user timing.','', 'The immutable manifest includes build/media/log/script hashes, before-image binding, exact candidate IDs and per-board limits. Native pixel failures against older references are not reported as overall test passes.','', '## Per-board scope and remaining gaps','', '| Board | Native result | Remaining gap |','|---|---|---|']
for j in m['journeys']:lines.append(f'| {j["component"]} | {j["status"]} | {j["remainingJourneyGap"]} |')
lines += ['', '## Publication','']
for key,value in publication.items():lines.append(f'- {key}: {value}')
lines += ['', '## Remaining ownership','', 'The parent commissions two new independent reviews. No score was assigned. A human owns merging after required checks and reviews; this agent did not merge or watch the PR. The known /more/troubleshooting chart-ownership gap is outside board scope and was not given an invented spec. The earlier hosted offline Numberlink SQLite eight-second fallback cause remains unproven; no bypass or retry was added. Board fixtures do not establish live transport, persisted end-to-end flows, app updates or live lexicon service behavior.']
